    "answer": {
      "short": "28 marbles in box A, 12 marbles in box B.",
      "worked": "The total number of marbles stays the same. Express both ratios with 40 total parts:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Original total parts} &= 7+3=10\\\\\n\\text{New total parts} &= 5+3=8\\\\\n\\text{Original A:B} &= 28:12\\\\\n\\text{New A:B} &= 25:15\n\\end{align*}$$\nBox A loses $28-25=3$ of these equal parts, representing the 3 transferred marbles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{1 part} &= 3\\div3=1\\text{ marble}\\\\\n\\text{Original box A} &= 28\\times1=28\\text{ marbles}\\\\\n\\text{Original box B} &= 12\\times1=12\\text{ marbles}\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
